new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f484371
--- /dev/null
+++ b/video/filter/vf_cudapass.c
@@ -0,0 +1,383 @@
+/*
+ * vf_cudapass — identity CUDA filter (VideoPlayerGold spike).
+ *
+ * Takes cuda[nv12|p010|...] frames from nvdec, copies every plane device to
+ * device into a filter-owned CUDA allocation that sits under a filter-owned
+ * AVHWFramesContext, and emits the copy as a cuda frame. It changes no pixel.
+ *
+ * Its whole purpose is to prove, in one build, everything a real GPU effect
+ * needs from mpv before any effect code is written:
+ *   - a native user filter registered and dispatched inside the chain
+ *   - borrowing the decoder's CUDA context (no second context, no host copy)
+ *   - output frames that hwdec_cuda (OpenGL/Vulkan interop) maps directly
+ *   - hot parameter changes through vf-command without a chain rebuild
+ *
+ * Driver entry points come from ffnvcodec's dynamic loader (nvcuda.dll /
+ * libcuda.so), so the cross build needs no CUDA toolkit.
+ *
+ * This file is part of mpv.
+ *
+ * mpv is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
+ * modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public
+ * License as published by the Free Software Foundation; either
+ * version 2.1 of the License, or (at your option) any later version.
+ *
+ * mpv is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
+ * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
+ * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
+ * GNU Lesser General Public License for more details.
+ *
